"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. Applies the given function object f to the projected result by proj of dereferencing each iterator in the range…"},{"label":"Parameters","note":"first, n, f, proj"},{"label":"Return value","note":"An object {first + n, std::move(f)}, where first + n may be evaluated as std::ranges::next(std::move(first), n) depending on iterator category."},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Exactly n applications of f and proj."},{"label":"Possible implementation"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"range-for loop(C++11)","note":"executes loop over range"},{"label":"ranges::for_each","note":"applies a function to a range of elements"},{"label":"for_each_n","note":"applies a function object to the first N elements of a sequence"},{"label":"for_each","note":"applies a function to a range of elements"}]}]},"standards":["C++11","C++17","C++20"],"wordCount":527,"codeBlockCount":3}
